---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../components/layout/Section.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
import ClassifiedBand from "../components/ui/ClassifiedBand.astro";
import PitchDeckNav from "../components/ui/PitchDeckNav.astro";
import CTA from "../components/ui/CTA.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/typography/Eyebrow.astro";
import Heading from "../components/typography/Heading.astro";
import Rule from "../components/typography/Rule.astro";
import "@/styles/global.css";
---

<Layout title="MI5 Strategic Assessment — Environmental Matrix">
  <ClassifiedBand label="TOP SECRET — MI5 STRATEGIC ASSESSMENT // ENVIRONMENTAL MATRIX" />

  <!-- ─── PAGE HEADER ─── -->
  <Section variant="black" spacing="sm">
    <Eyebrow>Strategic Assessment</Eyebrow>
    <Heading level={2} variant="section">The World & <em>Setting</em></Heading>
    <Rule />
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── TIMELINE BAND ─── -->
  <div class="band">
    <pre class="band-header">
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MI5 STRATEGIC ASSESSMENT // ENVIRONMENTAL MATRIX
TIMELINE: 1965 – 1970 // THE FIVE-YEAR METAMORPHOSIS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    </pre>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── SECTION 1: TWO LONDONS ─── -->
  <Section variant="dark" spacing="sm">
    <Eyebrow>Geography</Eyebrow>
    <Heading level={3} variant="section" class="world-title">Two <em>Londons</em></Heading>
    <Rule />
    <p class="prose world-prose">
      <em>Her Majesty's Displeasure</em> is set in the shifting fault lines
      of late-1960s London — a city actively tearing itself away from its
      imperial past. The series functions as a claustrophobic, dark workplace
      comedy split between two highly insulated, opposing bubbles: the rigid,
      silent, administrative halls of British power and the loud, chaotic,
      smoke-filled incubator of Abbey Road Studio Two.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── WORLD 1: THE CROWN ─── -->
  <div class="world-block world-block--crown">
    <div class="world-block__image-col">
      <div class="image-stack">
        <img src="/thepalace01.jpg" alt="Buckingham Palace — Cold Corridors" class="stack-img" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/thepalace02.jpg" alt="Ministry of Defence Briefing Room" class="stack-img" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/thepalace03.jpg" alt="Royal Architecture — Frozen in Time" class="stack-img" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="image-stack__label">BUCKINGHAM PALACE // MINISTRY OF DEFENCE // WHITEHALL</div>
    </div>
    <div class="world-block__text-col">
      <div class="world-block__badge">THE CROWN</div>
      <h3 class="world-block__title">The Symmetrical Vacuum</h3>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label">The Look</span>
        <p>Cold, sterile, desaturated wide-shots of Buckingham Palace corridors and Ministry of Defence briefing rooms. Every frame is a perfectly composed, melancholic still-life of imperial decay.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label">The Rule</span>
        <p>Absolute Wes Anderson-style symmetry. The architecture is massive, grand, and frozen in time. The human beings inside these frames are dwarfed by centuries of inherited stone — looking isolated, rigid, and deeply paranoid.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label">The Palette</span>
        <p>Desaturated greys, muted blues, pale yellows. The color slowly leaches out of these scenes as the series progresses, mirroring the moral decay of the conspiracy itself.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label">The Soundscape</span>
        <p>The clatter of a typewriter from an adjacent room. The tick of a grandfather clock. Footsteps echoing on marble. Silence that lasts one beat too long. The palace breathes in a different rhythm than the city outside its walls.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label">The Comedic Function</span>
        <p>The comedy comes from introducing visually chaotic elements — a clumsy spy, a joint passed in a bathroom, an avant-garde artist's screeching noise — into these rigidly composed, deadpan frames. The institution's perfect geometry is constantly polluted by the messy reality it tries to contain.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── WORLD 2: THE BAND ─── -->
  <div class="world-block world-block--band">
    <div class="world-block__text-col world-block__text-col--band">
      <div class="world-block__badge world-block__badge--band">THE BAND</div>
      <h3 class="world-block__title world-block__title--band">The Cluttered Canvas</h3>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label trait-label--band">The Look</span>
        <p>Warm, high-contrast, amber-tinted close-ups of Abbey Road Studio Two. The frame is packed with cigarette smoke, tangled microphone cables, half-empty teacups, lyric sheets scribbled on napkins, and glowing amplifier tubes.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label trait-label--band">The Rule</span>
        <p>Cluttered, living, and claustrophobic. The camera here breathes, moves, and feels fluid — capturing a volcanic creative explosion happening in real-time. Unmotivated pans, handheld urgency, crash zooms on a snare hit.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label trait-label--band">The Palette</span>
        <p>Warm ambers, saturated reds, golden hour tones. The palette shifts across the series — from the bright primary colors of 1965 pop to the darker, psychedelic hues of 1968–1970. The lighting grows harsher as the band fractures.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label trait-label--band">The Soundscape</span>
        <p>Studio chatter bleeding through headphones. The hum of an amp warming up. A guitar string snapping. Laughter, then an argument, then laughter again. Music being built from the inside out.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="world-block__trait">
        <span class="trait-label trait-label--band">The Comedic Function</span>
        <p>The comedy here is warmer, more human — the absurdity of four lads from Liverpool trying to make art while an empire conspires against them in a building a mile away. Every time MI5 tries to subtle-sabotage the creative process, the music just gets weirder and better.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="world-block__image-col">
      <div class="image-stack">
        <img src="/thebeatles01.jpg" alt="Abbey Road Studio Two" class="stack-img" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/thebeatles03.jpg" alt="The Beatles in Session" class="stack-img" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/thebeatles04.jpg" alt="Creative Chaos" class="stack-img" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="image-stack__label image-stack__label--band">ABBEY ROAD STUDIO TWO // APPLE CORPS // LONDON N.W.3</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── VISUAL COLLISION SPLIT ─── -->
  <Section variant="black" spacing="md">
    <Eyebrow>Visual Collision</Eyebrow>
    <Heading level={2} variant="section">When Worlds <em>Collide</em></Heading>
    <Rule />
    <p class="prose">
      The series' visual language is a deliberate, irreconcilable clash. Every
      scene that cuts between these two worlds reinforces the central dramatic
      irony: the state's machinery is enormous, ancient, and utterly incapable
      of understanding what it's trying to destroy.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <div class="collision-split">
    <div class="collision-half collision-half--crown-simple">
      <img src="/thepalace02.jpg" alt="Palace Interior" class="collision-img" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="collision-img-label">THE ESTABLISHMENT: ORDER</div>
    </div>
    <div class="collision-half collision-half--band-simple">
      <img src="/thebeatles07.jpg" alt="Beatles in Studio" class="collision-img" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="collision-img-label collision-img-label--band">THE REBELLION: CHAOS</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── MACRO TIMELINE ─── -->
  <Section variant="black" spacing="lg">
    <Eyebrow>Cultural Arc</Eyebrow>
    <Heading level={2} variant="section">From Medals to <em>Radicalism</em></Heading>
    <Rule />
    <p class="prose">
      The five-year narrative arc tracks the fastest, most volatile cultural
      transformation in modern British history. The series' visual palette
      evolves with it.
    </p>

    <div class="timeline-duo">
      <div class="timeline-era">
        <div class="timeline-era__year">1965</div>
        <div class="timeline-era__label">The Polite Mirage</div>
        <p>
          The era of the clean-cut "mop-tops." The band wears matching
          tailored collarless suits, accepts royal honors, and plays by the
          establishment's rules. The Crown believes they can be managed with
          subtle, polite bureaucratic "nudges."
        </p>
        <div class="timeline-era__img">
          <img src="/thebeatles05.jpg" alt="The Beatles — 1965" class="timeline-img" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-era timeline-era--late">
        <div class="timeline-era__year">1966 – 1967</div>
        <div class="timeline-era__label">The Psychedelic Rupture</div>
        <p>
          <em>Sgt. Pepper</em> convinces Philip the threat is real. The band
          experiments with LSD, Eastern philosophy, and avant-garde
          composition. The colors in their world begin to bleed outside the
          lines. MI5's "nudges" start claiming credit for chaos they didn't
          cause.
        </p>
        <div class="timeline-era__img">
          <img src="/thebeatles06.jpg" alt="The Beatles — 1967" class="timeline-img" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-duo">
      <div class="timeline-era timeline-era--late">
        <div class="timeline-era__year">1968 – 1969</div>
        <div class="timeline-era__label">The Fracture</div>
        <p>
          The White Album sessions. The illusion breaks. John brings Yoko
          to the studio. George grows frustrated with the songwriting monopoly.
          The band stops being a band and becomes a legal entity in dispute.
          Clive charts "Revolution 9" for seventy-two straight hours, convinced
          it contains encrypted Soviet launch codes.
        </p>
        <div class="timeline-era__img">
          <img src="/thebeatles08.jpg" alt="The Beatles — 1968" class="timeline-img" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-era">
        <div class="timeline-era__year timeline-era__year--final">1970</div>
        <div class="timeline-era__label">The Dissolution</div>
        <p>
          The rooftop concert. The failed assassination. The farcical collapse.
          The Beatles dissolve through their own dynamics, not Philip's
          masterful design. A lone madman in New York achieves in a single
          afternoon what the entire apparatus of the Crown could not
          accomplish in five years. The universe wins.
        </p>
        <div class="timeline-era__img">
          <img src="/misc-hmd01.jpg" alt="1970 — The End" class="timeline-img" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── KEY LOCATIONS ─── -->
  <Section variant="dark" spacing="lg">
    <Eyebrow>Geography</Eyebrow>
    <Heading level={2} variant="section">Key <em>Locations</em></Heading>
    <Rule />
    <p class="prose">
      The series moves between a handful of highly insulated, pressure-cooker
      environments — each with its own visual language, soundscape, and
      emotional temperature.
    </p>

    <div class="locations-grid">
      <div class="location-card">
        <div class="location-card__icon">🏛️</div>
        <h4>Buckingham Palace</h4>
        <p>The seat of the conspiracy. Philip's domain. Cavernous, silent, symmetrical. Every conversation echoes. Every piece of furniture is older than anyone in the room. The war room for a war nobody knows is being fought.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="location-card">
        <div class="location-card__icon">🎵</div>
        <h4>Abbey Road Studios</h4>
        <p>The creative incubator. Warm, cramped, alive. The place where the most influential music of the 20th century is being made while two men in suits sit in a car outside, taking notes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="location-card">
        <div class="location-card__icon">🏢</div>
        <h4>MI5 — Thames House</h4>
        <p>The bureaucratic engine. Fluorescent lights. Filing cabinets. Typewriters. The place where Clive files his "victory reports" and Nigel stares at the clock, counting the minutes to his pension.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="location-card">
        <div class="location-card__icon">✈️</div>
        <h4>Kenwood — Weybridge</h4>
        <p>John's suburban prison. A mock-Tudor mansion in the stockbroker belt. The place where a marriage unravels while an empire watches through the hedges. Psychedelic wallpaper meets post-war respectability.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="location-card">
        <div class="location-card__icon">🌿</div>
        <h4>Rishikesh, India</h4>
        <p>The operational dead zone. The Beatles meditate while MI5 agents sit in a sweltering hotel, unable to surveil anyone. The conspiracy's impotence exposed through spiritual tourism.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="location-card">
        <div class="location-card__icon">❄️</div>
        <h4>The Falklands — 1980</h4>
        <p>The epilogue. Cold storage at the bottom of the world. Two desks. One clock. A radio. The punchline to a five-year joke neither man finds funny.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── SATIRICAL CORE ─── -->
  <Section variant="paper" spacing="lg">
    <Eyebrow>Thesis</Eyebrow>
    <Heading level={2} variant="section">The Satirical <em>Core</em></Heading>
    <Rule />
    <p class="prose">
      As the counter-culture accelerates completely out of the state's
      control, Prince Philip's intelligence operation spirals from a petty
      exercise in domestic surveillance into a desperate, panicked thriller.
      The show captures the exact moment the British Empire realizes its
      grand, centuries-old machinery of control is entirely powerless against
      four working-class boys armed with feedback loops, Eastern philosophy,
      and a guitar amplifier.
    </p>

    <div class="misc-gallery">
      <img src="/misc-hmd02.jpg" alt="The Cultural Fault Line" class="misc-img" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/misc-hmd03.jpg" alt="Empire Meets Counterculture" class="misc-img" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/misc-hmd04.jpg" alt="The Machinery of Control" class="misc-img" loading="lazy" />
    </div>

    <div class="diagnostic-quote">
      <pre class="quote-mono">
DIAGNOSTIC: "The architecture of the palace was built to last a thousand years.
The music of Abbey Road was built to change the world by Tuesday."
      </pre>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── PITCH DECK NAV ─── -->
  <PitchDeckNav current="/world" />

  <!-- ─── FOOTER ─── -->
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ─── BAND ─── */
  .band {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--bg4);
  }

  .band-header {
    max-width: var(--container-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    letter-spacing: 0.04rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ─── WORLD PROSE ─── */
  .world-title {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .world-prose {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    color: var(--text4);
  }

  /* ─── WORLD BLOCKS ─── */
  .world-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .world-block--crown {
    background: var(--bg2);
  }

  .world-block--band {
    background: var(--bg1);
  }

  .world-block__image-col {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .image-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .stack-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 180px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
    filter: grayscale(30%) contrast(1.05);
    border: 1px solid var(--bg4);
  }

  .world-block--band .stack-img {
    filter: saturate(1.1) contrast(1.0) sepia(0.1);
  }

  .image-stack__label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--space-1);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    background: var(--bg3);
  }

  .image-stack__label--band {
    color: var(--color-amber);
    border-color: rgba(200, 168, 75, 0.2);
    background: rgba(18, 30, 18, 0.8);
  }

  .world-block__text-col {
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-5);
  }

  .world-block__text-col--band {
    order: -1;
  }

  .world-block__badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-blue);
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }

  .world-block__badge--band {
    border-color: var(--color-amber);
    color: var(--color-amber);
  }

  .world-block__title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.6rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text1);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .world-block__title--band {
    color: var(--text-accent);
  }

  .world-block__trait {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .trait-label {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.18rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }

  .trait-label--band {
    color: var(--color-amber);
  }

  .world-block__trait p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text5);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ─── VISUAL COLLISION SPLIT ─── */
  .collision-split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 2px;
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .collision-half {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .collision-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 300px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .collision-half--crown-simple .collision-img {
    filter: grayscale(40%) contrast(1.1) brightness(0.8);
  }

  .collision-half--band-simple .collision-img {
    filter: saturate(1.15) sepia(0.05);
  }

  .collision-img-label {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: var(--space-3);
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.22rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 5px 14px;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
    backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .collision-img-label--band {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
  }

  /* ─── TIMELINE ─── */
  .timeline-duo {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  .timeline-era {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue);
    padding: var(--space-4);
  }

  .timeline-era--late {
    border-left-color: var(--color-amber);
  }

  .timeline-era__year {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }

  .timeline-era--late .timeline-era__year {
    color: var(--color-amber);
  }

  .timeline-era__year--final {
    color: var(--color-red) !important;
  }

  .timeline-era__label {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .timeline-era p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text5);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .timeline-era__img {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .timeline-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 140px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--bg4);
    filter: grayscale(20%);
  }

  .timeline-era--late .timeline-img {
    filter: saturate(1.0) sepia(0.08);
  }

  /* ─── KEY LOCATIONS ─── */
  .locations-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin: var(--space-5) 0;
  }

  .location-card {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border: var(--border-faint);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    transition: transform 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease;
  }

  .location-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--text-accent-dim);
  }

  .location-card__icon {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .location-card h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text2);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-1);
  }

  .location-card p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text5);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ─── MISCELLANEOUS GALLERY ─── */
  .misc-gallery {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 4px;
    margin: var(--space-5) 0;
  }

  .misc-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 200px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
    filter: contrast(1.05);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
  }

  /* ─── DIAGNOSTIC QUOTE ─── */
  .diagnostic-quote {
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    background: var(--bg2);
  }

  .quote-mono {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.03rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-blue);
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
  }

  /* ─── RESPONSIVE ─── */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .world-block {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .world-block__text-col--band {
      order: 0;
    }

    .locations-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .misc-gallery {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .misc-img {
      height: 160px;
    }
  }

